.TH "waybar\-wwan" "5" "2026\-08\-08" "waybar\-wwan" "User Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- wwan module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBwwan\fR module for ModemManager.\&
.PP
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/waybar/config 
.br
Per user configuration file
.PP
.SH ADDITIONAL FILES
.PP
libmm\-glib lives in:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP 1. 4
/usr/lib/libmm\-glib.\&so or /usr/lib64/libmm\-glib.\&so
.IP 2. 4
/usr/lib/pkgconfig/libmm\-glib.\&pc or /usr/lib64/pkgconfig/libmm\-glib.\&pc
.IP 3. 4
/usr/include/libmm\-glib
.PD
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string  
.br
default: \fB{state}\fR 
.br
The format, how information should be displayed.\& This format is used when other formats aren'\&t specified.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-failed\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem cannot start.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-locked\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the SIM on the modem is locked.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-disabled\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is disabled.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-enabled\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is enabled, but isn'\&t registered to any carrier network.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-searching\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is looking for a carrier network to register to.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-registered\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is registered to a network, but no data connection is active.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-connected\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is registered to a network, and there is an active data connection.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-icons\fR: 
.br
typeof: array/object 
.br
Based on the current signal strength, the corresponding icon gets selected.\& 
.br
The order is \fBlow\fR to \fBhigh\fR.\& Or by the state if it is an object.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: true 
.br
Option to disable tooltip on hover.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\fR: 
.br
typeof: strirng 
.br
default: {state} 
.br
The format, how information should be displayed in the tooltip.\& This format is used when other formats aren'\&t specified.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\-failed\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem cannot start.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\-locked\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the SIM on the modem is locked.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\-disabled\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is disabled.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\-enabled\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is enabled, but isn'\&t registered to any carrier network.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\-searching\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is looking for a carrier network to register to.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\-registered\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is registered to a network, but no data connection is active.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\-format\-connected\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
This format is used when the modem is registered to a network, and there is an active data connection.\&
.PP
\fBinterval\fR: 
.br
typeof: integer 
.br
default: 5 
.br
The interval in which the WWAN information gets polled (e.\&g.\& carrier name).\&
.PP
\fBimei\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Select only the modem with the corresponding imei.\&
.PP
\fBpath\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Select only the modem with the corresponding hardware path.\&
.PP
\fBhide\-disconnected\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: true 
.br
Defines if the module should be hidden while the modem does not have an active data connection.\&
.PP
.PP
.SH FORMAT REPLACEMENTS
.PP
\fB{state}\fR: Modem state.\&
.PP
\fB{current_modes}\fR: List of all the currently active connection modes.\&
.PP
\fB{preferred_mode}\fR: The preferred connection mode in use.\&
.PP
\fB{signal_quality}\fR: Signal quality (0\-100).\&
.PP
\fB{operator_name}\fR: Name of the network operator.\&
.PP
\fB{icon}\fR: Icon selected from \fBformat\-icons\fR according to the signal quality.\&
.PP
\fB{power_state}\fR: Modem power state (On/Off/Low/Unknown).\&
.PP
\fB{imei}\fR: Modem equipment identifier (IMEI).\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"wwan": {
	"format": "{state}",
	"format\-disabled": "", // an empty format will hide the module
	"format\-locked": "SIM Locked",
    "format\-connected": "{operator_name} {preferred_mode} | {signal_quality}%"
	"tooltip\-format": "{preferred_mode}",
	"tooltip\-format\-connected": "{current_modes}",
	"hide\-disconnected": false
}
.fi
.RE
